    {
      "id": "c9f987722942647288857cfa11f2a184d820cb73",
      "individual_note": false,
      "resolvable": true,
      "resolved": true,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2227581874,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "I think, unfortunately, that this still gives the same error, because XML 1.0 does not allow control characters even in CDATA:\n\nhttps://www.w3.org/TR/xml/#sec-cdata-sect\n\ndefines CDATA to consist of Char, and Char is defined so that it doesn't include ESC or other ASCII control characters (beside tab, space, line feed, carriage return):\n\nhttps://www.w3.org/TR/xml/#NT-Char\n\nThe widely-unused XML 1.1 allows control characters to be specified via `&#x1b;` and similar, but XML 1.0 doesn't even allow that.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
